revision.text:
{{otheruses|the rewards system|the point of interest|Wizard's Vault (point of interest)}}

[[File:Wizard's Vault interface icon.png|right|link=]]
{{quotation|[https://www.guildwars2.com/en/news/new-rewards-in-guild-wars-2-secrets-of-the-obscure/ Official site]|The Wizard’s Vault is a new streamlined rewards system that combines the best elements of the daily login and daily achievement systems, allowing you to play Guild Wars 2 the way you want to–whether it’s [[PvE]], [[Player vs Player]], or [[World vs World]], or a mix–and earn a wide variety of exciting rewards for doing so.}}

{{icon|misc|Wizard's Vault icon.png}}[[Wizard's Vault]] is a rewards system available to all [[player]]s, replacing the previous daily [[login reward]] format and its generic [[Daily (achievements)|daily achievements]].<ref name="Discover WV">[https://www.guildwars2.com/en/news/discover-the-wonders-within-the-wizards-vault-in-guild-wars-2-secrets-of-the-obscure/ Discover the Wonders within the Wizard’s Vault in Guild Wars 2: Secrets of the Obscure], Guildwars2.com</ref> After selecting their choice of either PvE, PvP, WvW, or mixed objectives, players are awarded with [[Astral Acclaim]] for completing these tasks, which can be exchanged for various rewards, including some [[Gem Store]] items. Some Wizard's Vault tasks and rewards are exclusive to [[expansion]]s, but all types of accounts with a level 80 character have access to the feature and the currency.<ref name="New rewards"/>

== Overview ==
[[File:Wizards Vault Pane.jpg|thumb|Wizard's Vault panel]]
* Players receive new objectives to complete daily, weekly, with each quarterly release (called seasons), and certain [[festival]]s and [[bonus event]]s. Completing them grants {{Astral acclaim}} [[Astral Acclaim]]
** There is a soft limit of {{Astral acclaim|1300}} Astral Acclaim that a player can have at any given time. Players can only claim the rewards from Vault objectives while the Astral Acclaim in an account's wallet is below {{Astral acclaim|1300}}. Other sources, like [[100_Astral_Acclaim|an achievement that gives Astral Acclaim]], may still be able to go over the soft cap.
** Players will always receive at least one daily task in each selected category.
* If different players select identical categories and own the same expansions, they will receive the same objectives. Players with different expansions may see different objectives.
** Buying an expansion will display a different set of objectives '''immediately''', not at reset. Objectives which you have done before the purchase will only count for the progress if they are present in your new objectives list, too. Some of the new objectives might be partially or completely solved - it seems the game tracks your progress in the background. If you have already claimed a daily or weekly chest before the purchase, you will not be able to claim it again.
* Rewards refresh on a quarterly basis (indicated by the timer under the Special tab), but any Wizard’s Vault–exclusive cosmetic<ref name="official website about Wizard‘s Vault">[https://help.guildwars2.com/hc/en-us/articles/19617357502867-Secrets-of-the-Obscure-Wizard-s-Vault Secrets of the Obscure: Wizard's Vault], Guildwars2.com</ref> rewards simply move into the Legacy Rewards section of the vault, where they’ll remain available for the same type of currency indefinitely, at a slightly higher price than at their introduction.<ref name="official website about Wizard‘s Vault"/><ref name="New rewards" />
** The rewards are attainable through regular, normal play; there are no paid upgrades or progression skips, and the [[#Legacy Rewards|Legacy Rewards]] section exists to take the time pressure off and allow players to catch up if they take a break.<ref name="New rewards">[https://www.guildwars2.com/en/news/new-rewards-in-guild-wars-2-secrets-of-the-obscure/ New Rewards in Guild Wars 2: Secrets of the Obscure], Guildwars2.com</ref>
* Daily achievement points are still available, earned by completing Wizard's Vault daily objectives.
* [[File:Achievements Watch List.png]] Wizard's Vault objectives can be tracked, they however replace normal tracked [[achievement]]s in the UI.
** [[File:Swap to Achievements.png|25px|Swap to Achievements‎]] [[File:Swap to Wizard's Vault.png|25px|Swap to Wizard's Vault‎]] These buttons in the right top corner allows you to switch between the Achievement Watchlist and the Wizard's Vault Watchlist.
* The Wizard's Vault has three sections:
** {{icon|misc|Wizard's Vault Objectives.png}} [[#Objectives|Objectives]] — lists all currently available objectives, also includes timers
** {{icon|misc|Wizard's Vault Astral Rewards.png}} [[#Astral Rewards|Astral Rewards]] — lists all currently available seasonal rewards
** {{icon|misc|Wizard's Vault Legacy Rewards.png‎}} [[#Legacy Rewards|Legacy Rewards]] ‎— lists cosmetic rewards from previous seasons

== Objectives ==
{{see|Wizard's Vault/Easy objectives|Wizard's Vault/List of objectives#Daily|Wizard's Vault/List of objectives#Weekly}}

{{icon|misc|Wizard's Vault Objectives.png}} The objectives available depend on the game modes selected and owned [[expansion]]s. Two players with the same game modes selected and the same [[expansion]]s owned will have identical objectives, but having for example PvE and WvW chosen, your PvE objectives may be different to someone with only PvE chosen, or with only [[Guild Wars 2|Core]] content available.

=== Game mode selection ===
Upon opening the [[Wizard's Vault]], players are presented with a dialogue asking them to choose which game modes ([[PvE]], [[PvP]] & [[WvW]]) they would like to receive objectives for, allowing daily/weekly game modes to be selected independently. This selection can be changed at any time by clicking the [[File:Options Menu Bar icon.png|19px]] gear icon in the daily or weekly tabs. If any objectives have been claimed (other than the daily "Log in"), the change does not take effect until their respective refresh.

=== Refresh ===
Daily objectives refresh with the [[Server reset|daily reset]] every day at {{UTC time|00:00}}, and weekly objectives refresh every {{UTC time|Monday 07:30}}.

{{Wizard's Vault objective countdowns|2026-09-01T16:00Z}}

=== Daily ===
Four random daily objectives will be selected from the chosen set of gameplay options every day, plus a fixed "Log in" objective. Each daily objective rewards {{Astral acclaim|10}} on completion, while the Log In daily awards {{Astral acclaim|5}}.

Completing four objectives of the day will reward a [[Wizard's Vault Daily Completion Chest|daily completion chest]] containing other rewards and {{Astral acclaim|20}}. Players will also earn the [[Wizard's Vault: Daily Completionist]] daily achievement, rewarding {{ap|10}} until a {{ap|15000}} limit is reached. This limit combines the current daily achievement and a number of past daily and monthly categories. (Refer to [[Achievement#Trivia]] for a list of them.)

=== Weekly ===
Eight random weekly objectives will be selected from the chosen set of gameplay options at the start of each week. Each weekly objective rewards {{Astral acclaim|50}} upon completion.

Completing six of the weekly objectives will reward an additional [[Wizard's Vault Weekly Completion Chest|weekly completion chest]] containing other rewards and {{Astral acclaim|450}}.

{{Weekly Wizard's Vault}}

See [[Extended Weekly Wizard's Vault]] for additional upcoming weeks.

=== Special ===
{{see|Wizard's Vault/Historical special objectives}}
The special category contains additional objectives which refresh with each season (usually quarterly), and temporary [[festival]] and [[special event]] objectives. These objectives do not change by game modes selected nor [[expansion]] ownership. Most of these objectives can only be completed by playing content related to the latest expansion.

{{Wizard's vault objectives widget}}

